\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Probe fine-tuning on corrected OH labels across data fractions. The zero-shot--to--5\% jump ($+$25.2\,pp) and rapid convergence toward structural GB (0.992 on conf${\geq }$2) demonstrate that label quality, not model capacity, was the transfer bottleneck. Under old (corrupted) labels, 5\% fine-tuning reached only 0.570.}}{12}{table.caption.33}\protected@file@percent }
