\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Extended LLM-as-judge evaluation on SWE-Agent conf${\geq }$2 ($N{=}1{,}824$). All Claude rows use the same model; the performance gain comes from prompting strategy. CoT alone yields gains comparable to few-shot ($+$8.7\,pp vs.\ $+$8.9\,pp over zero-shot); combining them (five-shot-CoT) adds a further 4.8\,pp, suggesting complementary mechanisms. $^\ddagger $30 structural features provided as formatted text in the LLM prompt; performance degrades below pure few-shot (0.7514), indicating structural signals require engineered classifiers. $^\dagger $GPT-5.5: 22.4\% of responses (408/1,824) failed to parse; macro-F1 is computed over the 1,416 windows with valid outputs. On silver, the best LLM (0.799) trails structural features (0.995); on gold, the ranking reverses (LLM 0.910 vs.\ GB 0.839; \S  \ref {sec:gold_set}). Total API cost across all configurations: \$131.90.}}{14}{table.caption.36}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:llm_extended}{{9}{14}{Extended LLM-as-judge evaluation on SWE-Agent conf${\geq }$2 ($N{=}1{,}824$). All Claude rows use the same model; the performance gain comes from prompting strategy. CoT alone yields gains comparable to few-shot ($+$8.7\,pp vs.\ $+$8.9\,pp over zero-shot); combining them (five-shot-CoT) adds a further 4.8\,pp, suggesting complementary mechanisms. $^\ddagger $30 structural features provided as formatted text in the LLM prompt; performance degrades below pure few-shot (0.7514), indicating structural signals require engineered classifiers. $^\dagger $GPT-5.5: 22.4\% of responses (408/1,824) failed to parse; macro-F1 is computed over the 1,416 windows with valid outputs. On silver, the best LLM (0.799) trails structural features (0.995); on gold, the ranking reverses (LLM 0.910 vs.\ GB 0.839; \S \ref {sec:gold_set}). Total API cost across all configurations: \$131.90}{table.caption.36}{}}
